{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>I will intoxicate My arrows with blood.</b> And how is it possible for arrows to become intoxicated from blood? Rather: I am intoxicating others with what My arrows do." "<b>And My sword shall eat flesh.</b> And is it possible for a sword to eat flesh? Rather: I am feeding others with what My sword kills — as it is said, ״Son of man, say to every bird of wing and to every beast of the field, etc. — you shall eat the flesh of mighty men and drink the blood of the princes of the earth, etc., and you shall eat fat to satiety and drink blood to intoxication״. Thus it is expounded in Sifrei." "<b>From the blood of the slain and the captive.</b> From what they did to the slain of My people and to the captives of My people." "<b>From the head of the long-haired ones of the enemy.</b> Strip it of its consonants as: from the long locks of the head of the enemy." "And Rabbi Nehemiah expounds it concerning the nations, and this is what it says." "<b>Lest they say:</b> The nations <b>'Our hand is raised,'</b> etc." "<b>For a nation lost, counsels are they:</b> The seven nations lost the seven commandments that I gave them." "<b>If they were wise:</b> If the nations had been wise, <b>they would understand this:</b> what is expounded as follows — how could one of them pursue a thousand of Israel today, when formerly it was the reverse?" "<b>They would understand their latter end:</b> The punishments destined to come upon them for having enslaved Israel, as it is written: וחש עתידות למו." "<b>Were it not that their Rock sold them:</b> And why did it happen to them that one of them pursues a thousand of them? <b>Were it not that their Rock</b> — the Rock of Israel — sold them into our hands. This is what the seven nations should have understood." "<b>For not like our Rock is their rock.</b> For their rock is not powerless as our Rock, and because of this our enemies, Israel, were judges in the past, and they would judge us and rule over us." "<b>For from the vine of Sodom is their vine.</b> And why did their rock sell them? Rather, surely because <b>from the vine of Sodom is their vine</b>, and from the planting of Amorrah are they, whose <b>grapes are grapes of rosh</b>, etc., as it is written, 'their sin is like Sodom's' — that is to say, there is no good in them but all are evil, and the Holy One, blessed be He, does not demand retribution for their insult." "<b>Is it not laid up with Me.</b> What they said about My people — that their vine is from the vine of Sodom — is sealed with Me, for it is not so; rather, about them it is said, 'and I, I planted you a choice vine,' etc." "<b>Vengeance and recompense are Mine.</b> To exact from the seven nations. <b>When their foot slips</b> — of the seven nations. <b>For near is the day of their calamity</b> — of the seven nations. <b>And what is impending hastens to them</b> — to the seven nations." "<b>For He will see, etc.</b> And why will He avenge them? <b>For He will see</b> the enemy, <b>that their hand</b> — of Israel — <b>has failed.</b>" "<b>And he said.</b> And the enemy said <b>where is their Elohim</b> — that of Israel." "<b>Let them arise and help you.</b> For thus the enemy says, and therefore He will judge their cause." "<b>See now</b> etc. As I explained above." "<b>And none delivers from My hand.</b> Corresponding to what the enemy said: let them arise and help you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:32.942544593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}